This repository contains a new Rust implementation of Markitai's public
conversion interfaces. Project source is licensed under MIT; see LICENSE.
The standard license text and original project attribution are retained.

Document parsers and runtime dependencies are resolved in Cargo.lock. The
initial implementation uses anydoc, pdf-inspector, scraper/html5ever, htmd,
mail-parser, reqwest/rustls, and other Rust crates under their respective
licenses. It does not bundle or invoke the reference Python PDF engine.

Before distributing a release, generate the resolved dependency inventory
and include each dependency's applicable license/copyright notices. A crate's
metadata license identifier alone is not the complete notice bundle.
Reference test fixtures remain in the reference checkout; audit reports record
fixture hashes and never redistribute them as newly authored fixtures.

The embedded browser workspace includes Marked 18.0.14 (MIT) and DOMPurify
3.4.16 (Apache-2.0). Their complete notices are in vendor/web/marked-LICENSE
and vendor/web/DOMPurify-LICENSE. Download provenance, upstream package
integrity and embedded-file hashes are recorded in vendor/web/provenance.json.
